- Use the relevant row for neutral Header and scrim roles. The suggested accent is a reference for an explicitly requested palette change only; otherwise implement the supplied `--accent`. These are starting points for this template, not universal industry rules.

| Industry / direction | Header surface / text | Hero scrim RGB | Optional accent recommendation |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Enterprise AI, SaaS, data, or unspecified — graphite | `#141820` / `#F5F7FA` | `12, 16, 24` | Cool teal `#65D6CE` |
| Finance, legal, consulting — warm ivory | `#F3EFE7` / `#20282C` | `20, 29, 32` | Deep teal `#176B65` |
| Architecture, property, luxury — limestone | `#E8E2D8` / `#292723` | `26, 25, 23` | Bronze `#A97545` |
| Climate, energy, sustainability — forest charcoal | `#18231E` / `#F2F4EC` | `16, 28, 22` | Lime `#C8DC83` |
| Healthcare, wellbeing — soft mineral | `#EDF3F0` / `#203A35` | `18, 35, 31` | Teal `#227C73` |
| Creative, media, culture — ink and coral | `#211E23` / `#FAF4EF` | `25, 21, 26` | Coral `#F28A73` |

- Default for enterprise/data copy: graphite Header, near-white menu text, natural media colors with a charcoal readability gradient, and the supplied accent on the primary CTA. Even if `--bg` is vivid blue, do not produce a blue Header plus a blue/purple Hero wash. If the chosen neutral Header still merges into the Hero, use the warm-ivory Header/text pair for visible light/dark separation.
- Preserve natural media colors. Use neutral scrims for readability: start around 0.60–0.78 opacity behind copy, fading to 0.08–0.24 over open background areas; adjust locally for contrast rather than increasing a saturated overlay across the whole frame. Do not use multiply/color blend modes or a blue-to-purple filter over the entire visual.
- Reserve saturated brand color for the primary CTA, small indicators and restrained hover/focus details. Keep secondary CTA and navigation surfaces neutral. Give the navigation CTA its own contrasting neutral foreground/background pair so it remains distinct from both the menu surface and the Hero CTA.

