### Signature Composition — Full-Screen Video Across Header and Hero
- Required hierarchy: `.hero-shell > .hero-media (poster + video), .hero-scrim, header, main.hero-content`. In scrolling mode, continuation sections are siblings after `.hero-shell`. Keep semantic Header and Main landmarks; do not nest Header inside Main.
- `.hero-shell { position: relative; isolation: isolate; }`; `.hero-media` and `.hero-scrim` use `position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none`. Layer media at `z-index: 0`, scrim at `1`, foreground copy at `2`, Header at `3`, and the open mobile menu above all of them. Avoid negative z-index.
- The video and poster fill the same shared shell: `position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: center; border-radius: 0`. Do not apply a fixed aspect ratio, a card, a separate media column or a video block below the CTA at any breakpoint.
- The same footage media layer continues beneath Header and Hero without resizing or restarting at their boundary. The Header has its own visibly distinct neutral surface; this deliberate color separation does not split the underlying full-screen media. Use one continuous neutral scrim across the shell with an alignment-aware gradient behind copy, fading into the visible footage. Use `--scrim-rgb` from the color direction, not the saturated `--bg` or `--accent`; do not cover the footage with an opaque full-width copy panel.
- Header stays in the first grid row in normal flow. Give Hero content `padding-block: clamp(32px, 5svh, 72px)` so the first copy element is at least 32px below the Header's bottom (24px below on mobile). This gap is foreground breathing room over the same video, never an empty solid band or a downward offset of the video itself.
- Center the copy vertically within the remaining Hero row when space allows. H1 max-width 560px; subhead max-width 52ch. Center alignment places copy over the center of the footage; split alignment places copy in the left portion while the right remains open footage imagery, without creating a second media column.
- Below 640px keep exactly the same edge-to-edge background behind Header and copy; adjust crop with `object-position` if needed. Use 20px content gutters and wrapping CTAs. Never stack a poster window below the text.
- Keep the Hero free of stock-footage UI: no “City study” label, atmospheric-footage caption, Asset Details button, information icon, media toolbar, sound control or Pause/Play button. Keep source and license records in project documentation only.

- Template-specific art direction: Use fine architectural rules and generous negative space in the foreground; keep perspective lines visible without framing the video.

